# Production checks — edit this file and push to run them.
#
# MODE (first non-empty, non-comment line):
#
#   report                   READ-ONLY. Runs both checks and prints the result.
#                            Writes nothing. Safe to run at any time, as often
#                            as you like.
#
#   backfill-graph-tenant    WRITES. Stamps tenantId onto graph nodes that
#                            predate the write paths doing it, attributing each
#                            one from its Postgres mirror row. Idempotent, and
#                            it refuses to guess an owner for anything whose
#                            mirror row is gone. Re-reports afterwards.
#
# The two checks:
#
#   1. Role-flip preflight — can the backend run as `databridge_app` with
#      row-level security actually enforced? Today it runs as a superuser,
#      which bypasses RLS entirely, so every tenant_isolation policy in the
#      database is inert. The preflight reports GO only when every RLS-enabled
#      table has a policy and the role holds every grant it needs.
#      See docs/runbooks/db-role-flip.md.
#
#   2. Graph tenant backfill (report mode) — how many Neo4j nodes still lack
#      `tenantId`. Every write path stamps it now, but nodes written before
#      that do not carry it. A tenant predicate must NOT be added to the read
#      queries until this reports zero: an unstamped node does not leak once
#      predicates exist, it silently disappears from its owner's catalog.
#
# Both read the same production secrets deploy.yml already uses. Neither
# touches business data — the preflight reads the catalog, the backfill reads
# tenant ids from mirror rows.
